Source: pg-tre
Section: database
Priority: optional
Maintainer: Ruohang Feng <rh@vonng.com>
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13), postgresql-all (>= 217~), autoconf, automake, libtool, gettext, git, m4, libicu-dev
Standards-Version: 4.7.2
Rules-Requires-Root: no
Homepage: https://codeberg.org/gregburd/pg_tre

Package: postgresql-PGVERSION-pg-tre
Architecture: any
Provides: postgresql-pg-tre
Depends: ${postgresql:Depends}, ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Description: Native index access method for approximate regular expressions for PostgreSQL PGVERSION
 pg_tre provides a native text index access method for approximate regular
 expression matching, backed by compressed trigram postings and the TRE
 matcher. It also supports regular expressions, LIKE and edit-distance
 ordering. It uses generic WAL and needs no shared preload.
